    "label": "Computing Specialization",
    "notes": "Majors in Mathematics/Economics may select a Computing specialization by satisfying all the requirements for a bachelor’s degree in the major; and completing the following courses, with a minimum grade of C– in each course and a combined grade-point average of at least 2.0. Students must petition for admission to the program and are advised to do so after they complete Program in Computing 10B (petitions should be filed in the Mathematics Department Student Services Office). Students graduate with a bachelor’s degree in mathematics/economics and a specialization in Computing."
   }
